  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Two angles whose measures add up to \\(90^\\circ\\) are complementary, and \\(30^\\circ+60^\\circ=90^\\circ\\). Both \\(45^\\circ+135^\\circ\\) and \\(100^\\circ+80^\\circ\\) equal \\(180^\\circ\\), so these pairs are supplementary; \\(20^\\circ+80^\\circ=100^\\circ\\).",
